urant here that people can enjoy in  this community because I think we've  lost so many of them especially black  owned restaurants in this community we  need something that represents people if  it's not African culture or black  American culture you need something that  represents them represents us I seen  that from this community  really do support and want me to  continue while this neighborhood grows  what do you hope your impact is on the  community I want people to eat better to  have the opportunity to have something  that is hosting I want people to know  that we're here and we're not just here  to like extract from the community we  will actually want to give back it's why  when the corona virus pandemic took its  toll  open Crum began working with three  nonprofits to provide more than 300  meals a week for those who need the most  that's hard for businesses to do at a  time like this where obviously you  already are being stretched is it it is  but it gives you so much more back  there's more to having a restaurant than  just making money if you can give us  someone a meal and they're hungry that's  something that we should be doing it's  an extension he says of open Crum open  prom to me means technique food should  in my opinion take time this is one of  the most important ingredients that you  have and it's that time and that time  together when you were referencing when  you were a kid yeah it's like my mom's  always taking our time and fear I love  every step when you spend so much time  on something it really does show up that  people feel and taste that love people  do it you can't really duplicate it and  honestly this is a family business  everyone is involved in it in that  community now Jeff is a part of that  family as well just fantastic I want  some of that fish Dana all right really  good stuff it was good
 

